  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The quadratic equation \r\n$2 x^{2}-\\left(a^{3}+8 a-1\\right) x+a^{2}-4 a=0$ has roots of opposite sign. Then,",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "2uXGN",
      "text": "$a \\leq 0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "EMBAF",
      "text": "$0     < a < 4$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "kdMjC",
      "text": "$4 \\leq a     < 8$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Y6YLy",
      "text": "$a \\geq 8$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since, roots are opposite sign.\r\nProduct of the roots $\\leq 0$ $\\begin{array}{ll}\\Rightarrow & a^{2}-4 a     < 0 \\\\ \\Rightarrow & a(a-4) < 0 \\\\ \\Rightarrow & 0 < a < 4\\end{array}$",
    "image": null
  },
